Title: Bi-Microporous Metal-Organic Frameworks with Cubane [M4(OH)4] $(M=M i$ , Co) Clusters and Pore Space Partition for Electrocatalytic Methanol Oxidation Reaction
Cubane $[N i_{4}(O H)_{4}]$ MOF for MOR: A new 3D microporous Ni-MOF containing cubane $[N i_{4}(O H)_{4}]$ cluster has been prepared and for the first time used as electrocatalyst for methanol oxidation reaction (MOR). The optimal hybrid material shows impressive performance in electrocatalytic MOR activity including a high mass specific peak current of $527~\mathsf{m A}\mathsf{m g}^{-1}$ and excellent peak current density $(29.8\mathsf{m A}\cdot\mathsf{c m}^{-2})$ at a very low potential (0.6V).
